        "Tags": "instrument, harmony, generative, arpeggiator, xy, pressure",
        "Preferred Panels": "blocks",
        "name": "Spiegel 12",
        "description": "An interpretation of Laurie Spiegel's Music Mouse for Plinky 12. The right 12x16 field is the \"mouse\": your finger position (x = columns, y = rows) drives two interlocking voice pairs (X pair + Y pair, interval apart), all snapped to a harmonic mode. The left strip is the \"keyboard hand\": six pressure pads (Vibrato, Tremolo, Filter, Accent, Delay, Random) shape the sound while you play, and tap pads choose mode, motion (parallel / contrary), treatment (Chord / Arp / Line / Improv), articulation, 10 patterns, interval, transpose, octave offsets and 3 sounds. Random varies the notes you are playing (neighbour / third / fifth in the scale), like Accent it only affects the played notes. Note changes are quantised to the clock (Off or 1/16): the cursor you touch is only adopted on the next grid line. Filter and Delay share one per-note slot, the harder-pressed pad wins. Runs on the free-running clock, no transport needed.",
